{#-
  The feed: every world as a card, shown after <main> on every page but the two that list every
  page themselves (sitemap.html, moods.html). It is the one index of worlds the site has, and
  _data/worlds.json is the one place the list and every world's name are kept: a world is added,
  renamed or retired there, and this include, the site map and the mood atlas all follow.

  One flat list, no groups. Each card carries the world's orientation over its name -- the same
  phrase the persona card reads a visitor as -- and the world's own palette, through data-mood
  (_sass/_mood.scss), so the feed is a mosaic of the moods the worlds answer to. The world a
  visitor is already on is left out of its own feed.

  What the template writes is the whole of what a visitor without scripting gets: a column grid
  of plain cards, every one a link, so the reachability axiom holds and index.html's own markup
  links every world. js/feed.js then lays the cards out as masonry columns, paints each card
  through its module in js/modules/, moves the world the visitor's reading opens onto to the
  front, and keeps dealing fresh cards -- the things the worlds make -- as the visitor scrolls,
  without end. The sentinel at the bottom is what tells it to deal more.

  The headings are real (h2, then h3 per card), so a visitor listening to the page hears its
  shape.
-#}
{%- set here = (page.filePathStem | replace('/', '')) + '.html' if page else '' -%}
<section class='feed' id='feed' aria-labelledby='feed-title'>
  <div class='feed-head'>
    <h2 class='feed-title' id='feed-title'>every world</h2>
    <p class='feed-note'>{{ worlds.worlds.length | words | capitalize }} worlds and no default, each a card, with the things they make dealt in between. Over each name is who the site would send there: open the one that fits, or the one that does not, and keep scrolling.</p>
  </div>
  <div class='feed-grid' id='feed-grid'>
{%- for world in worlds.worlds %}
{%- if world.file != here %}
    <article class='card card-world' data-world='{{ world.file }}' data-mood='{{ world.mood }}' data-name='{{ world.name }}' data-orientation='{{ world.orientation }}'>
      <a class='card-link' href='{{ siteRoot }}{{ world.file }}'>
        <div class='card-media' style='aspect-ratio: {{ world.aspect }}'><canvas class='card-canvas' aria-hidden='true'></canvas></div>
        <div class='card-body'>
          <p class='card-overline'>{{ world.orientation }}</p>
          <h3 class='card-title'>{{ world.name }}</h3>
          <p class='card-text'>{{ world.what }}</p>
        </div>
      </a>
    </article>
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class='feed-sentinel' id='feed-more' aria-hidden='true'></div>
  <p class='feed-foot'><a href='{{ siteRoot }}sitemap.html'>site map</a></p>
</section>
